#. Description of the plugin
#: capybara-seo-lead-source-tracker.php
msgid ""
"Captures UTMs and click IDs, keeps them across page visits, and adds them to "
"your WhatsApp messages via an auto-injected floating button, your existing "
"buttons, and/or a shortcode — combinable. <a href=\"options-general.php?"
"page=capysele-lead-source-tracker\">Configure the plugin</a>."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: capybara-seo-lead-source-tracker.php
msgid "Henry Silva"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:8
msgid ""
"Captures UTM parameters and click IDs, keeps them across page visits with "
"the attribution model you choose (last click by default, or first click), "
"and automatically includes them in the WhatsApp message of your floating "
"button, your existing buttons, and/or the [capysele_button] shortcode."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:14
msgid "Save changes"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:20
msgid "Quick setup"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:22
msgid "Set your WhatsApp number and save (section 1)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:23
msgid ""
"Turn on the button placement(s) that match your situation, following the "
"guide in section 2."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:24
msgid ""
"Choose the attribution model in section 3: last click credits the most "
"recent identifiable source before the WhatsApp click; first click keeps the "
"first one captured. Save, then reload the site page before testing."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:25
msgid ""
"Test with a URL that includes UTM parameters, for example ?"
"utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=test"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:28
msgid "Placeholder reference"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:46
msgid ""
"Use {exit_page} for the complete URL where the visitor clicks. "
"{landing_page} is a legacy alias that returns the same click-time URL and "
"remains available for existing templates."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:47
msgid ""
"{captured_at} is the date of the selected capture: the initial one with "
"first click, the most recent one with last click. If there is no valid "
"capture, it shows the time of the WhatsApp click instead, which is not "
"evidence of a real capture."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:48
msgid ""
"Use {exit_page_title} for the title of the page where the visitor clicks "
"(the browser tab title), read at the moment of the click. Use the title, the "
"URL, or both; if the page has no title, its line is removed from the message."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:50
msgid "How the channel is detected"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:51
msgid ""
"{channel} describes the source selected by the configured attribution model "
"(the latest or the first identifiable entry), not necessarily the visit "
"where they click. Rules are checked in this order:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:53
msgid ""
"Google Ads or Meta Ads: paid UTM parameters (e.g. "
"utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc) or a click ID (gclid, gbraid, wbraid, "
"fbclid)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:54
msgid "Organic: utm_medium=organic."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:55
msgid ""
"AI platforms (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Copilot, Perplexity): detected from "
"the referrer domain when there is no click ID and utm_medium is empty or "
"\"referral\"."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:56
msgid "Referral: utm_medium=referral, or a visit from another website."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:57
msgid ""
"Organic: a visit from a search engine (Google, Bing, Yahoo, DuckDuckGo, "
"Baidu, Yandex, Ecosia)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:59
msgid ""
"With no UTMs, click IDs or external referrer, no channel is assigned and the "
"{channel} line is removed."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:61
msgid "How long attribution is kept"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:67
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Attribution is kept in this browser's local storage for %d day, counted from "
"the selected capture. With last click, each new identifiable entry (UTMs, "
"click IDs or an external referrer) replaces the whole record and restarts "
"the period. With first click, later entries don't replace the source or "
"restart the period. In both models, visits without source signals and "
"WhatsApp clicks never renew it. Once it expires, the plugin stops using that "
"record and deletes it the next time it runs; a new identifiable visit can "
"then start a new attribution period."
msgid_plural ""
"Attribution is kept in this browser's local storage for %d days, counted "
"from the selected capture. With last click, each new identifiable entry "
"(UTMs, click IDs or an external referrer) replaces the whole record and "
"restarts the period. With first click, later entries don't replace the "
"source or restart the period. In both models, visits without source signals "
"and WhatsApp clicks never renew it. Once it expires, the plugin stops using "
"that record and deletes it the next time it runs; a new identifiable visit "
"can then start a new attribution period."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:75
msgid ""
"Attribution is stored per browser and device; it does not identify the same "
"visitor across devices."
msgstr ""

